{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016KbVLtacAtueSeUepUJSaY","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: always-persist-solver-solutions\ndescription: Never run MOSP solvers with solutions_dir=None; witness orderings must always be cached to disk\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 33a51384-932b-453c-9bf1-f79a57a6b34e\n  modified: 2026-09-16T16:09:26.027Z\n---\n\nNever call `solve_mosp_sat` (or wire a batch runner) with `solutions_dir=None`. Solutions must always be persisted to `solutions/`. Do not add an opt-out flag for this.\n\n**Why:** A MOSP solve is expensive — minutes to hours per hard instance — and the witness ordering *is* the result. The MOSP value alone cannot be independently verified or reused, so discarding the ordering means the work has to be redone. In the first full benchmark sweep I passed `solutions_dir=None` in the worker, and ~1,300 solved instances had their orderings thrown away before the user caught it.\n\n**How to apply:** In `benchmarks/solve_parallel.py`, `solutions_dir` is a required `Path` defaulting to `solutions/`, never `Optional`. Persisting also makes re-runs cheap: `solve_mosp_sat` verifies and reuses a cached solution, so raising the timeout only costs time on instances that previously timed out. In tests, pass a `tmp_path` solutions dir rather than disabling caching.\n\nRelated: [[mosp-sat-strategy]]\n----GEN\ndef generate_random_instance(\n    n_customers: int,\n    n_patterns: int,\n    density: float = 0.3,\n    seed: int | None = None,\n    name: str | None = None,\n) -> MOSPInstance:\n    \"\"\"Generate a random MOSP instance with given density.\n\n    Each entry M[i][j] is 1 with probability `density`, independently.\n    Rows/columns that are all-zero are given at least one random 1 to ensure\n    every customer needs something and every pattern is needed by someone.\n\n    Args:\n        n_customers: Number of customers (rows).\n        n_patterns: Number of patterns (columns).\n        density: Probability each entry is 1.\n        seed: Random seed for reproducibility.\n        name: Instance name.\n\n    Returns:\n        A MOSPInstance with the generated binary matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n\n    if name is None:\n        name = f\"random_{n_customers}x{n_patterns}_d{density:.2f}_s{seed}\"\n\n    matrix = (rng.random((n_customers, n_patterns)) < density).astype(np.int8)\n\n    # Ensure no all-zero rows (every customer needs at least one pattern)\n    for i in range(n_customers):\n        if matrix[i].sum() == 0:\n            j = rng.randint(0, n_patterns)\n            matrix[i, j] = 1\n\n    # Ensure no all-zero columns (every pattern is needed by at least one customer)\n    for j in range(n_patterns):\n        if matrix[:, j].sum() == 0:\n            i = rng.randint(0, n_customers)\n            matrix[i, j] = 1\n\n    return MOSPInstance.from_matrix(matrix, name=name)\n\n\n----CO\n----SIG\n557:def solve_mosp_exact(\n558-    instance: MOSPInstance,\n559-    *,\n560-    procedure: str = DEFAULT_PROCEDURE,\n561-    solutions_dir: Path | str | None = SOLUTIONS_DIR,\n562-    upper_strategy: str = \"cs-dfs\",\n563-    time_budget: float | None = None,\n564-    max_nodes: int | None = None,\n565-    stats: dict | None = None,\n566-) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n567-    \"\"\"Solve MOSP to optimality with the project's default decision procedure.\n568-\n569-    This is the entry point to reach for. `solve_mosp_sat` remains what its name\n570-    says -- the SAT encoding, reachable here as `procedure=\"sat\"` -- and is worth\n571-    running when a checkable proof object matters, since a refutation from the\n572-    customer search is not a DRAT proof (`CLAUDE.md`, item 7).\n573-\n574-    The value returned is `max_open_stacks` of the ordering, re-simulated on the\n575-    original instance rather than taken from the search's own accounting: the\n576-    closing-order measure can over-charge, and a witness that does not simulate\n577-    to its claimed value is a bug that must not reach the corpus.\n578-\n579-    Args:\n580-        procedure: \"csearch\" (default) or \"sat\".\n581-        upper_strategy: the named heuristic supplying the starting upper bound.\n582-        time_budget: seconds for the descent. Without one the search runs to a\n----GI\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.pytest_cache/\nbenchmarks/instances/*.mosp\n*.egg-info/\n\n# Lean 4 build artifacts\nlean/.lake/build/\nlean/.lake/config/\nlean/.lake/packages/\n\n# Lean build outputs and fetched dependencies\nlean/.lake/\n*.so\n*.drat\nproofs/\n.venv-cpsat/\n\n# Regenerated from the corpus in seconds; not worth versioning\nlearning/data/\nlearning/models/\n\n# Unattended re-certification logs and results\nrecertify/\n----N\nn_customers\n9.0       10\n10.0    1604\n13.0       1\n14.0       3\n15.0    1194\n17.0       3\n18.0       4\n19.0       5\n20.0    1298\n21.0       1\n24.0       1\n25.0       6\ndtype: int64\n----LOAD\n12\n32\n 22:22:45 up 13 days,  4:17,  1 user,  load average: 5.20, 8.97, 9.91","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dec266e6-6179-4276-aeb1-1b2d1d4d29a0","uuid":"1905344c-436e-47dd-af7d-43300cce01fa","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:22:45.714Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nname: always-persist-solver-solutions\ndescription: Never run MOSP solvers with solutions_dir=None; witness orderings must always be cached to disk\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 33a51384-932b-453c-9bf1-f79a57a6b34e\n  modified: 2026-09-16T16:09:26.027Z\n---\n\nNever call `solve_mosp_sat` (or wire a batch runner) with `solutions_dir=None`. Solutions must always be persisted to `solutions/`. Do not add an opt-out flag for this.\n\n**Why:** A MOSP solve is expensive — minutes to hours per hard instance — and the witness ordering *is* the result. The MOSP value alone cannot be independently verified or reused, so discarding the ordering means t